md-mode
*******

`M-x md-mode' in a Markdown buffer replaces the window with the
rendered document: proportional body text, scaled headings, drawn
tables, quoted passages with a bar down their left, syntax-highlighted
code and inline images.  `M-x md-mode' again, or `q', returns to the
source.

This is not syntax highlighting.  `markdown-mode' makes the *source*
prettier and leaves every `#', `**' and `[label](url)' on screen,
which is the right choice for editing.  md-mode is for reading: the
markup goes away and a document appears.

